error[ffi_unknown_tag]: `opaque191_t` is `struct opaque_s191` in `fixedbugs-191-types.h`, and the header gives it no fields — clang read the header and cannot lay the type out
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-191-a-partial-record-of-an-opaque-typedef.hero:16:12
     |
  16 |     record opaque191_t partial  #~ ffi_unknown_tag
     |            ^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: the header keeps the type opaque: a program never holds one by value, only C's pointer to it, which is a HANDLE. Drop the field block and give the record the typedef as its tag, `record opaque191_t tag opaque191_t` (§ 13)
